.page factor 1 print the prime factors of numbers

# SYNOPSIS
*factor* _NUMBER_...

# DESCRIPTION
`factor` prints each _NUMBER_ followed by a colon and its prime factors, in ascending order, with repeated factors repeated. Numbers up to 2^64 are accepted, but large ones with big prime factors take a long time because the method is trial division.

# EXAMPLES
    factor 360
    factor 9 97 1001

# SEE ALSO
seq(1), expr(1)
